Z||000000||saleenfiero||09-04-2001||08:11 PM||||I know this has been talked about before, now that I am eyeing up a fiero parts car with no keys to it, how can I hotwire the thing?  Don't worry, I'm not trying to start a fiero theft ring, just would like to maybe buy this thing and get some interesting info at the same time.  Direct email would be fine.  Thanx for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||09-04-2001||08:43 PM||||If you just want to start it, pull the plug on the ignition switch and either jump it or plug in another one and go.<P>If you need to steer it, pull the steering wheel and use some duct tape to hold the lock pin out of the lock plate. Or keep going and just put in a new lock cylinder. I did this on a 87 Caprice I bought at a police auction with no keys and drove it home.<P>Cheap & easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||09-04-2001||09:09 PM||||Isn't it possable to just smash a flat blade into the ignition and then twist? I know my friend did this to his old beater civic when he lost the keys. I thought this could be done to all older GM's.<P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg">  <P>{edit... typo}<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||Leadfoot||09-04-2001||10:50 PM||||Usually the tumblers are so warn that any late GM key works.  Just a little wiggle with the key should do it.||||reg||1
